# 09b distinguishing ablations of clean C

Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree of C, runs this packet's own
cases against it, and is reverted before the next. The worktree is a temporary checkout; this
repository's working tree is never modified, and its status is printed at the end. The point is
012's requirement that the oracle reject a plausible wrong implementation. Each block prints the
one-file diffstat, then every failing case by name.

